# Build outputs
out/
build.log

# live-build working artifacts (never commit; regenerated every build)
.build/
cache/
chroot/
binary/
local/

# Test harness output
test/screen.png

# Remotion promo: dependencies and rendered artifacts (keep the source)
promo/node_modules/
promo/out/
promo/.remotion/
test/launcher-zoom.png
test/screen.png
.firebase/

# Local-only credentials and key material — never commit.
#
# Broadened from two exact filenames to the shapes those files take, because
# naming one file only protects that one name. The repository is public, so a
# credential committed here is a credential published: rotate it, do not just
# delete the file, because the object survives in history.
r2-credentials.txt
r2.env
.env
.env.*
*-PRIVATE-*.asc
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
rclone.conf
# Cloudflare Wrangler's local secret store and config. .dev.vars holds the
# Stripe key while developing the gate Worker; wrangler.toml can carry account
# ids and bindings. Neither is currently in the tree — these are here so that
# creating one does not get staged by a `git add -A`.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
wrangler.toml

# Local editor/tooling settings. Personal to whoever is working on the tree and
# of no use to anyone cloning it.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Debug leftovers. Reading a Debian package's contents (to check what
# live-build actually does, or what a KDE theme actually ships) means
# `apt-get download` in whatever directory you happened to be in, and the .deb
# lands in the repo root. They are 200 KB each and belong to nobody.
# kde-style-breeze-data_4%3a6.3.5-1_all.deb was tracked from an earlier session
# and nothing referenced it; it has now been untracked, which is what this note
# used to ask for.
/*.deb

# The built APT repository. Regenerated in full by packages/build-repo.sh from
# config/includes.chroot, which is the single source of truth — committing it
# would add 5 MB of .deb to history on every release to store something that
# rebuilds in seconds. Build it before deploying the site.
site/repo/
